WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.851
By now, most film fans know that when the
credits roll on a Marvel Studios movie, the

00:00:04.851 --> 00:00:06.709
real fun is about to begin.

00:00:06.709 --> 00:00:11.430
That's because Marvel loves to set up future
franchise installments with teasers, Easter

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.219
eggs, and inside jokes "hidden" in scenes
during the credits.

00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:20.160
Usually, this means one or two small bits
during or after the credits, but with Guardians

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.560
of the Galaxy Vol. 2, writer-director James
Gunn has taken things to a whole new level

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.790
with five — yes, five! — credits scenes.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:33.400
Some are important, and some are just goofy,
but either way, we've got you covered with

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.960
explanations for every credits scene in Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 2.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.020
"Who else is gonna do it?"

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.480
"Awesome!"

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.460
Oh, and just so everyone's on the same page...spoilers
ahead.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.680
The Arrow

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.070
In the first bonus scene, Yondu's right hand
man Kraglin wears his former captain's robotic

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.130
fin to try and harness the power of his whistle-controlled
arrow.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:59.120
Of course, it goes horribly wrong.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.370
It looks like a funny scene, but actually
this is all a very complicated Easter egg

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:09.550
referencing the ascension of Kang the Conqueror
in Avengers Forever #9, and… no, just kidding.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.770
This scene is exactly what it seemed like:
a funny one-off joke.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:16.790
Hey, not every scene has to be filled with
secret meaning — okay?

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.680
The Original Guardians

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.160
Unlike the first credits scene, the second
is actually jam-packed with Marvel Comics

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.160
lore.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.650
Those Ravagers who show up for Yondu's funeral?

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:31.990
Some of them are actually members of the original
Guardians of the Galaxy team from the 1970s

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:32.990
comic books.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:39.330
Stakar, Martinex, Charlie-27, and Aleta are
all original flavor Guardians, while Mainframe

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.510
and Krugarr are also important characters
in the old school Guardians of the Galaxy

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:44.890
comic book universe.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:49.979
And considering the big name actors Marvel
signed up for the roles, like Sylvester Stallone,

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.720
Michelle Yeoh, and Ving Rhames, chances are
pretty good we're going to see a lot more

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.640
of these guys in future movies.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.770
Even if Stallone doesn't have the best track
record with comic book movies.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.292
"Why did you judge me?"

00:02:02.292 --> 00:02:03.292
"You killed innocent people."

00:02:03.292 --> 00:02:04.680
"The means to an end."

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.620
"You started a massacre!"

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.420
"I caused a revolution!"

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.680
"You betrayed the law!"

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.720
"Lawwwwww!"

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.020
Adam Warlock

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:15.020
If you were wondering why the people in your
theater erupted with screams of pure joy during

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:20.180
the third credits scene, the answer is Adam
Warlock, the mystery being inside the metal

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.700
cocoon built by the vengeful high priestess,
Ayesha.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.210
Marvel fans have been eagerly awaiting Warlock's
arrival in the movie universe because the

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:33.390
gold-skinned cosmic savior has been a key
player in basically every important Thanos

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.630
storyline in comics history.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:41.060
Adam Warlock is Thanos' archenemy, an avatar
of life dedicated to stopping Thanos and his

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.340
obsession with death.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:48.050
With Thanos set to finally take center stage
in 2018's Avengers: Infinity War, fans have

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:52.390
been wondering how Marvel would manage to
tell the story without Adam Warlock.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:56.230
Now we can all finally rest easy — if we
can stop freaking out.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.360
I am Groot

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.400
The fourth credits scene is pretty much just
a self-explanatory joke about Baby Groot growing

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.090
up to become Teen Groot.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:08.270
We're not sure if this means Teen Groot will
be in the sequel, or if this is a bridge to

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.360
explain why he's all grown up as Adult Groot
in the team's next appearance.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.090
But considering this brief clip is funnier
than just about any half-hour family sitcom

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.950
on primetime television right now, we can't
be the only ones hoping ABC develops a Growing

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.760
Up Groot spinoff, right?!

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:31.780
Stan the Man

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:36.330
For nearly 20 years now, Stan Lee has been
making cameos in Marvel movies.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:41.230
As a result, a fan theory developed along
the way that Stan isn't actually playing different

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:46.290
characters, but instead is a disguised member
of the alien race known as The Watchers, who

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.819
observe and record stories of mankind without
interfering in events.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:55.910
Now Lee and director James Gunn have confirmed
it with a fantastic bit where Stan is telling

00:03:55.910 --> 00:04:00.720
a group of Watchers about all the stories
he's participated in — which, of course,

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.510
are the other Marvel movies.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:07.300
It further proves what we've known all along:
Stan truly is The Man.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:12.820
"You know, I guess one person can make a difference.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:14.860
Enough said."

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:18.829
Thanks for watching!

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:21.659
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:21.659 --> 00:04:24.110
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

